{"id":1839768,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-23T22:52:10.997Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"}],"homepage":"https://cubana455.com/","id":1839768,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"es","original_title":"Cubana 455","overview":"Based on newly declassified documents, “Cubana 455” examines the sabotage of a Cuban civilian airliner off the coast of Barbados on October 6, 1976. The documentary follows the victims’ families, showing how they have persevered for more than forty-five years, still hoping for a glimmer of justice. It features interviews with the victims’ loved ones, a former CIA agent, a Venezuelan journalist, a CARICOM ambassador, a Cuban historian, the lawyer who represented Cuba before the United States, and three counter-revolutionaries involved in the sabotage.  “Cubana 455” portrays the dignity and strength of the Cuban people, who have suffered irreparable harm as a result of an act of terrorism—an act sponsored by those who claim to be fighting against terrorism. The documentary supports the CARICOM proposal to designate October 6 as an International Day Against Terrorism.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/qjbOPEm2F0HLGulCNURD5zOWZda.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":5175,"logo_path":"/685bT26uK9vuaCwf2Hylufdb4yI.png","name":"ICAIC","origin_country":"CU"},{"id":321063,"logo_path":null,"name":"ConeXión Aztlán-Cuba","origin_country":""},{"id":321064,"logo_path":null,"name":"New Vista Communications, LLC","origin_country":""},{"id":321065,"logo_path":null,"name":"Changó Media","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"CU","name":"Cuba"},{"iso_3166_1":"US","name":"United States of America"}],"release_date":"2023-09-06","revenue":0,"runtime":163,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Spanish","iso_639_1":"es","name":"Español"},{"english_name":"English","iso_639_1":"en","name":"English"}],"status":"Released","tagli